From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 01:48:44 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: enable the FRITZ!Box 7590's third PCIe port

RC0 and RC1 arrive from seale_avm.dtsi and carry this board's two
QCA9984 radios. RC2 is the board's own, and behind it is the VRX518 DSL
companion, 8086:09a9, with an 8 MiB prefetchable BAR0 that fits the
48 MiB window with room over.

No driver in this tree claims that device, so this enables an
enumeration and nothing more: the part appears in lspci and then sits
idle, with no DMA, no interrupts and no firmware download. It is worth a
status and three properties anyway. This is the first PCIe of any kind
on the GRX550, and RC2 is a third independent exercise of the root
complex glue, the config accessors and the serdes PHY on a die none of
them has run on before -- as well as the only thing that drives the
endian syscon's RC2 inbound-swap bit, which is what makes the
board-to-board register comparison complete rather than two thirds of
one.

That swap bit is the one real PCIe difference between the two boards.
The FRITZ!Box 7560 clears it; this board does not. The vendor clears it
from a file that reaches the FRITZ!Box 7560 only through the GRX350
common include, and the GRX550 chain does not pull that file in -- not
on this board, not on any other, and not in the release where the file
is present to be pulled. So the shared setting stands here.

Which value a VRX518 actually wants cannot be settled on this board,
because nothing crosses the link. Following the vendor is the safer of
the two guesses; the FRITZ!Box 7560's value describes a different chip
with a different driver.

The radios get no child node, here or anywhere. ath10k takes board and
calibration data from firmware files and reads nothing out of DT, so
there is nothing for one to say.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts
index 7a4e3a009602..ce4799246b02 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts
@@ -216,6 +216,18 @@ partition@1500000 {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * RC0 and RC1 carry the two QCA9984 radios; RC2 carries a VRX518 with no
+ * in-tree driver. Inbound byte swapping stays on: the SoC is big-endian and
+ * the DesignWare core is not.
+ */
+&pcie2 {
+	status = "okay";
+	intel,inbound-swap = <1>;
+	intel,outbound-swap = <0>;
+	reset-gpios = <&gpio0 16 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+};
+
 /*
  * Both USB host controllers. The vendor's HW226 chain carries no status
  * override on either of them, where the FRITZ!Box 7560's grx350_common.dtsi disables
